{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"text":" lists the systems of one frame or step. When it runs, it decides the order from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what you wrote and the constraints you added, and it runs the systems that can’t affect one","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another at the same time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Order-Systems","level":3,"text":"Order Systems","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, adjusted by ordering constraints. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system after another, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves it before one; every other system keeps its written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place. A constraint that names a type with no system in the schedule is ignored. Constraints that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a cycle trap, and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" instead, for systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or constraints that come from configuration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Run-Systems-Conditionally","level":3,"text":"Run Systems Conditionally","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips a system unless a condition on the world holds, such as the world holding no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Paused"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. On a nested schedule, it applies to each of the nested schedule’s systems. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system checks its conditions at the start of the wave it runs in, so a system that changes what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a condition reads affects the systems in later waves. A condition must read only what each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s access lists."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Understand-Waves","level":3,"text":"Understand Waves","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"conflict"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" runs the systems in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"waves"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": each wave holds the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose earlier conflicting and ordered systems have run, and its systems run at the same time. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes, so a system in the same wave doesn’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another’s spawns, despawns or inserts. To see them, order it after the system that queued them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The world ends as though the systems had run one after another, in order. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs the same waves one system at a time, with the same result. Use it to step through a system in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a debugger, or to rule out running at the same time as the cause of a problem.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system’s access comes from its parameters, with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" macro, or from an "},{"code":"access","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you declare by hand. A system without one may change anything, so it runs alone. In debug"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds, a system that reaches a type its access doesn’t list traps, so run a schedule’s tests in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"debug."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Find-Unordered-Conflicts","level":3,"text":"Find Unordered Conflicts","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on how they happen to be written, which a later edit can change by accident.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" lists those pairs. Order each pair, or mark it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" when either order is right, and check in a test that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list stays empty.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Group-Systems-into-Sets","level":3,"text":"Group Systems into Sets","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names a group of systems, so a constraint can refer to all of them at once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Declare one as an empty enumeration. A system joins it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inSet(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a nested schedule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inSet(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for all of its systems. Every system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is a set too, holding each system of that type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following schedule groups gravity and movement into a physics set that doesn’t run while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the game is paused, and scores after every physics system:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Schedule {","        Gravity()","        Movement().after(Gravity.self)","    }","    .inSet(Physics.self)","    .runIf { world in !world.resources.contains(Paused.self) }","    Scoring().after(Physics.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\"","print(frame.ambiguities().isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Profile-a-Schedule","level":3,"text":"Profile a Schedule","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Insert a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile"},{"type":"text","text":" resource into a world, and every schedule that runs on it records each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s runs and times. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes a schedule’s dependency graph in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"DOT language, so Graphviz can draw why systems run in the order they do and which can run at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"title":"Systems","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem/ambiguous(with:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns this system, also free to run in either order with every system in each of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given sets."}],"role":"symbol","title":"ambiguous(with:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem\/ambiguous(with:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguous","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"kind":"text","text":": repeat (each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":").Type) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV","text":"ScheduledSystem"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"kind":"symbol","title":"CyclicOrdering","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"title":"ambiguities()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"title":"Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"abstract":[{"text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Declaring Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"abstract":[{"text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"System","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it read results and take part in a step."}],"title":"Driving a World from an App","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/writeDOT(to:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Writes the schedule’s dependency graph in the DOT language, for drawing with Graphviz.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"writeDOT(to:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/writedot(to:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeDOT","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Runs each system once on a world, running systems that don’t depend on each other at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}],"title":"run(on:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/runSerially(on:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Runs each system once on a world, one system at a time.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"runSerially(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/runserially(on:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runSerially","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"role":"symbol","title":"System()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/init(checked:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a schedule of the given systems, throwing an error if their ordering constraints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a cycle."}],"title":"init(checked:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/init(checked:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checked"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV","text":"ScheduledSystem"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems14CyclicOrderingV","text":"CyclicOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"defaultImplementations":1,"kind":"symbol","title":"access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","type":"topic","role":"symbol","required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}]}}}